247
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:31,161
This guy's got help. Tell me when the asset's in the nest.

248
00:23:35,542 --> 00:23:37,442
Get me a feed in there!

249
00:23:37,544 --> 00:23:40,707
I want Grab Team C in there. Tell me what's going on.

250
00:23:48,025 --> 00:23:49,686
Team Four is mobile.

251
00:24:28,695 --> 00:24:30,287
Jesus Christ.

252
00:24:31,364 --> 00:24:33,332
That's Jason Bourne.

253
00:24:33,433 --> 00:24:36,459
He's picking us apart. Do you think he's the source?

254
00:24:36,669 --> 00:24:38,261
He's gotta be.

255
00:24:41,174 --> 00:24:44,371
Block all the exits. Give the asset a green light.

256
00:24:45,712 --> 00:24:47,646
Take them both out.

257
00:25:05,131 --> 00:25:06,792
Stay there.

258
00:25:07,667 --> 00:25:11,501
I'm gonna get us out of here. You gotta do exactly what I say.

259
00:25:11,971 --> 00:25:14,633
Listen to me! This isn't some story in a newspaper.

260
00:25:14,741 --> 00:25:17,801
This is real. You understand me?

261
00:25:30,123 --> 00:25:31,249
Call all agents back.

262
00:25:31,357 --> 00:25:33,848
Give Bourne's location at the back of the store to the asset.

263
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:34,927
Yes, sir.

264
00:25:53,446 --> 00:25:55,710
Kill the cameras.

265
00:26:02,021 --> 00:26:03,716
ROSS: Bourne. Wait. Something's not right.

266
00:26:03,823 --> 00:26:06,291
I can see the entrance from here. If I go now, I can make it.

267
00:26:10,430 --> 00:26:11,522
Bourne?

268
00:26:11,631 --> 00:26:13,360
Just stay where you are.

269
00:26:13,566 --> 00:26:15,625
ROSS: I don't think we should wait!

270
00:26:17,003 --> 00:26:18,937
I think someone's coming.

271
00:26:19,038 --> 00:26:21,404
I'm going for it. No, no, no, no, no!

272
00:28:05,111 --> 00:28:06,874
We have a situation.

273
00:28:13,519 --> 00:28:15,214
Director Kramer would like to see you.

274
00:28:15,321 --> 00:28:18,858
We need to get those warrants... He said it's urgent.

275
00:29:17,350 --> 00:29:21,116
REPORTER: What the police will tell me is that they believe the victim is 35-year-old

276
00:29:21,220 --> 00:29:26,525
Simon Ross, a well-known journalist based here in London with the Guardian newspaper.

277
00:29:26,525 --> 00:29:29,085
It appears that he was gunned down

278
00:29:29,195 --> 00:29:31,823
right in the middle of the Waterloo Station concourse

279
00:29:31,931 --> 00:29:37,334
around 3:45 this afternoon in full view of hundreds of commuters.

280
00:29:37,336 --> 00:29:38,860
Over the years, he's uncovered a lot of

281
00:29:40,039 --> 00:29:41,904
unsavory stories about terror

282
00:29:42,008 --> 00:29:45,239
that have upset certain Western governments and...

283
00:30:08,339 --> 00:30:10,569
Hi, how are you? Right over there?

284
00:30:10,641 --> 00:30:11,835
All right.

285
00:30:12,638 --> 00:30:14,037
Good morning, sir. Can I take your order? Yes.

286
00:30:14,140 --> 00:30:18,975
I'll have the Heart-Healthy omelet with goat cheese and peppers, please.

287
00:30:19,078 --> 00:30:20,943
Anything for you, ma'am? Just coffee, please.

288
00:30:21,047 --> 00:30:23,447
Are you sure? I'm buying. I'm good.

289
00:30:25,785 --> 00:30:29,221
So, when the Director called and it was suggested that we bring you on...

290
00:30:29,322 --> 00:30:32,257
Suggested? You sure it was just a suggestion?

291
00:30:39,432 --> 00:30:44,301
You know, it's funny how different things look depending on where you sit, right?

292
00:30:44,704 --> 00:30:46,934
I look at this as a favor for you, Pam,

293
00:30:47,039 --> 00:30:50,270
giving you an opportunity to complete some unfinished business.

294
00:30:50,376 --> 00:30:51,843
Meaning?

295
00:30:51,911 --> 00:30:55,347
Bourne. He's here. He's a threat.

296
00:30:55,815 --> 00:30:57,806
And we both want the same thing.

297
00:30:57,917 --> 00:31:00,408
But we both go about it in two very different ways.

298
00:31:00,519 --> 00:31:03,010
The past is past, Pam. All right?

299
00:31:04,023 --> 00:31:05,490
We were careless in Stockholm.

300
00:31:05,558 --> 00:31:07,185
So what was Waterloo? Just careless again?

301
00:31:07,293 --> 00:31:10,626
We had a leak. A serious national security situation.

302
00:31:10,730 --> 00:31:13,563
Bourne showed up on our surveillance and we had very little time to react.

303
00:31:13,666 --> 00:31:15,930
And a reporter got killed.

304
00:31:16,035 --> 00:31:18,936
Bourne saw us coming. The question is what was he doing there?

305
00:31:19,038 --> 00:31:20,437
No, the real question is how you managed

306
00:31:20,539 --> 00:31:23,007
to get into a firefight at a public train station.

307
00:31:23,109 --> 00:31:26,169
You know as well as I do decisions made in real time are never perfect.

308
00:31:26,278 --> 00:31:30,339
Don't second-guess an operation from an armchair.

309
00:31:34,487 --> 00:31:36,580
I'll see you at the office.

310
00:31:36,989 --> 00:31:38,923
Enjoy your egg whites.

311
00:31:58,911 --> 00:32:00,378
VOSEN: People!

312
00:32:00,446 --> 00:32:03,574
This is Pamela Landy and her associate, Tom Cronin.

313
00:32:03,682 --> 00:32:05,980
She's gonna be quarterbacking the search effort.

314
00:32:06,085 --> 00:32:07,552
Say your names. State your specs, please.

315
00:32:07,653 --> 00:32:11,521
Well, let's do names later, okay? What's Bourne's last fixed position?

316
00:32:11,624 --> 00:32:13,387
JIMMY: London, 1200 Zulu.

317
00:32:13,492 --> 00:32:15,323
Status. What is he? Armed? Wounded?

318
00:32:15,428 --> 00:32:17,953
JIMMY: Alive, mobile and unknown.

319
00:32:18,064 --> 00:32:19,861
Do we have an ECHELON package? WOMAN: Yes.

320
00:32:19,965 --> 00:32:21,830
Why isn't it on? We were waiting.

321
00:32:21,934 --> 00:32:24,164
Waiting? For what? What... Listen,

322
00:32:24,270 --> 00:32:27,262
people, do you have any idea who you're dealing with?

323
00:32:27,373 --> 00:32:28,499
This is Jason Bourne.

324
00:32:28,607 --> 00:32:30,404
You are nine hours behind the toughest target you have ever tracked.

325
00:32:32,344 --> 00:32:36,713
Now, I want everyone to sit down, strap in and turn on all you've got.

326
00:32:37,817 --> 00:32:39,512
That would mean now!

327
00:32:39,618 --> 00:32:41,017
Thank you.

328
00:32:41,120 --> 00:32:42,519
Give me a team deployment plan.

329
00:32:42,621 --> 00:32:45,715
I want everything you got on Ross on screen one.

330
00:32:54,867 --> 00:32:56,801
(CALLING BELL SOUNDING)

331
00:33:08,180 --> 00:33:09,704
BRIAN: Sir, I think we have something.

332
00:33:09,815 --> 00:33:11,715
We just hacked Ross' e-mail account at the Guardian.

333
00:33:11,817 --> 00:33:14,411
Found a round-trip ticket to Turin, Italy, yesterday.

334
00:33:14,520 --> 00:33:17,114
0800 arrival, 1205 departure.

335
00:33:17,223 --> 00:33:20,715
I think we can be pretty certain that Bourne's not your source, then.

336
00:33:20,826 --> 00:33:21,850
How?

337
00:33:21,961 --> 00:33:24,452
Ross's call to his editor where he said he'd just met the source

338
00:33:24,563 --> 00:33:27,555
took place just after his Turin flight landed.

339
00:33:27,666 --> 00:33:29,793
He met his source in Turin. So?

340
00:33:29,902 --> 00:33:32,393
What? So, what? Bourne met Ross in Turin for breakfast

341
00:33:32,505 --> 00:33:35,770
and then at noon the same day Bourne calls Ross to demand a meet at Waterloo?

342
00:33:35,875 --> 00:33:37,866
Maybe they were even on the same flight.

343
00:33:38,315 --> 00:33:39,646
Pull up everything you've got.

344
00:33:39,778 --> 00:33:43,009
Cross-check the secure cell phone usage of everyone with SCI clearance

345
00:33:43,115 --> 00:33:46,209
against all calls going in and out of Turin, Italy, the morning Ross was there.

346
00:33:46,318 --> 00:33:49,810
This guy you're after is a CIA operative with clearance above top secret.

347
00:33:49,922 --> 00:33:52,618
He's committing treason by talking to Ross.

348
00:33:52,725 --> 00:33:53,714
Do you really think while doing that

349
00:33:53,826 --> 00:33:55,885
he's gonna use a cell phone that he knows we can track?

350
00:33:55,995 --> 00:33:59,453
Zero results on the cross-check. So, you got any better ideas?

351
00:33:59,565 --> 00:34:01,692
Yeah, look at all the people whose cell phones were switched off

352
00:34:01,800 --> 00:34:03,427
the entire period Ross was in Turin.

353
00:34:03,536 --> 00:34:05,299
I mean, if your people are on their phones as much as mine,

354
00:34:05,404 --> 00:34:07,736
the list should be pretty small.

355
00:34:12,344 --> 00:34:16,007
Three names. Tom Brewster, Jack Boulin and Neal Daniels.

356
00:34:16,115 --> 00:34:18,879
Okay, now check everything in Ross' apartment against those names.

357
00:34:18,984 --> 00:34:23,148
Check for common patterns. Look for anything that indicates who Ross met.

358
00:34:23,255 --> 00:34:25,519
Pull up his socials. Pull it up.

359
00:34:25,624 --> 00:34:28,616
See those documents? CRONIN: Break it.

360
00:34:29,295 --> 00:34:30,387
Over here. What is that?

361
00:34:31,664 --> 00:34:34,326
All right. Right there. Initials.

362
00:34:34,433 --> 00:34:37,129
Pull that up. Bring that up on main.

363
00:34:41,173 --> 00:34:42,640
Neal Daniels.

364
00:34:42,741 --> 00:34:45,835
He's station chief in Madrid, isn't he? Yeah.

365
00:34:49,748 --> 00:34:51,579
All right, call the RSO at the embassy.

366
00:34:51,684 --> 00:34:54,050
Have them take Daniels into custody, if he is there.

367
00:34:54,153 --> 00:34:56,986
Anna, get grab teams to the Calle Norte safe house.

368
00:34:57,089 --> 00:34:59,580
Send them in heavy. Tell them we'll assist with the entry.

369
00:34:59,692 --> 00:35:03,184
Heavy? Daniels isn't really that much of a... I'm worried about Bourne.

370
00:35:03,295 --> 00:35:04,762
If he is not the source,

371
00:35:04,863 --> 00:35:07,331
then he is after the source, the same as we are.

372
00:35:41,166 --> 00:35:44,158
ETA, Team Two. Three minutes to destination, sir.

373
00:36:07,993 --> 00:36:11,986
DR. HIRSCH: Your mission will save American lives.

374
00:36:16,435 --> 00:36:19,996
Really give yourself to this program.

375
00:36:20,839 --> 00:36:22,363
I can't.

376
00:36:22,474 --> 00:36:24,066
DR. HIRSCH: You can.

377
00:37:01,680 --> 00:37:04,012
Sir, they're at the front door.

378
00:37:22,534 --> 00:37:24,434
Five seconds. Put it up live.

379
00:37:33,016 --> 00:37:34,347
We're in.

380
00:37:37,950 --> 00:37:39,747
The alarm's down.

381
00:37:40,419 --> 00:37:41,909
That's gotta be Bourne.

382
00:37:55,401 --> 00:37:56,993
The safe is empty. Shit.

383
00:37:57,102 --> 00:37:58,865
Looks like he left in a hurry.

384
00:37:58,971 --> 00:38:01,572
Track Daniels' passports. Stand by.

385
00:38:33,806 --> 00:38:35,330
(WHISPERING) Hammond.

386
00:38:59,731 --> 00:39:01,494
God damn it! Get a backup team in there!

387
00:39:13,078 --> 00:39:16,138
Get me a secure line in there. Get the second team over there now!

388
00:39:26,325 --> 00:39:28,293
What are you doing here?

389
00:39:29,761 --> 00:39:32,059
I was posted here after Berlin.

390
00:39:35,300 --> 00:39:37,029
Where's Daniels?

391
00:39:39,371 --> 00:39:41,236
Where is he?

392
00:40:05,898 --> 00:40:07,559
Who is this?

393
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:09,831
This is Nicky Parsons.

394
00:40:11,637 --> 00:40:13,571
She was Tread stone. Logistics.

395
00:40:13,672 --> 00:40:16,800
She was with us when we hunted Bourne in Berlin.

396
00:40:21,013 --> 00:40:23,208
Nicky, I need to do an ID challenge.

397
00:40:23,315 --> 00:40:25,044
Code in, Sparrow.

398
00:40:35,127 --> 00:40:36,355
Response, Everest.

399
00:40:41,466 --> 00:40:45,562
Nicky, this is Noah Vosen. How long have you been on-site?

400
00:40:45,671 --> 00:40:47,536
I just walked in.

401
00:40:48,407 --> 00:40:52,104
We have two officers on-site. Are you in contact with them?

402
00:40:55,480 --> 00:40:58,745
They're down. Unconscious but alive.

403
00:41:03,021 --> 00:41:05,888
Any sign of Neal Daniels? No.

404
00:41:06,592 --> 00:41:08,685
Nicky, this is Pam Landy.

405
00:41:09,561 --> 00:41:13,861
We have reason to believe there's a connection between Neal Daniels and Jason Bourne.

406
00:41:15,567 --> 00:41:19,503
Bourne? You're still looking for Bourne? I thought that case was closed.

407
00:41:19,605 --> 00:41:22,403
No, some people are convinced he's still a threat.

408
00:41:22,507 --> 00:41:24,975
I disagree, but to find out I need to talk to him.

409
00:41:25,043 --> 00:41:26,908
Hold on, Nicky.

410
00:41:28,213 --> 00:41:30,443
What the hell are you doing? I'm trying to send him a message.

411
00:41:30,549 --> 00:41:32,881
You don't think Bourne is a threat? He just took out two more of my men.

412
00:41:32,985 --> 00:41:34,577
The only way this has a happy ending, Noah,

413
00:41:34,686 --> 00:41:35,880
is if we bring him in alive.

414
00:41:35,988 --> 00:41:37,888
He is going after Daniels.

415
00:41:37,990 --> 00:41:39,685
He wants revenge, Pam, and the only realistic way

416
00:41:39,791 --> 00:41:41,782
to end this is to eliminate the threat.

417
00:41:41,893 --> 00:41:43,827
How long until backup?

418
00:41:45,130 --> 00:41:47,724
Nicky, I need you to stay put and secure the premises.

419
00:41:47,833 --> 00:41:51,667
Backup will be arriving in approximately one hour. Do you copy?

420
00:41:54,673 --> 00:41:57,001
NICKY: Copy, sir. (PHONE BEEPING)

421
00:42:00,979 --> 00:42:03,379
How long do I have? Three minutes.

422
00:42:05,984 --> 00:42:07,849
My car's outside.

423
00:42:09,221 --> 00:42:11,189
I know where Daniels is.

424
00:42:22,934 --> 00:42:25,767
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

425
00:42:29,946 --> 00:42:31,413
Come on.

426
00:42:32,177 --> 00:42:34,609
Two minutes to destination, sir. WILLS: Grab Teams A and B...

427
00:42:35,414 --> 00:42:36,506
Where was Daniels headed?

428
00:42:36,615 --> 00:42:40,949
At 8:00 this morning, he wired $100,000 to a bank account in Tangier.

429
00:42:41,787 --> 00:42:45,621
Right, that's 300 miles away. If we hurry, we can make the morning ferry.

430
00:42:46,792 --> 00:42:47,759
Where are you parked?

431
00:42:47,859 --> 00:42:51,090
To the right, 20 meters, north side of the street.

432
00:42:56,768 --> 00:42:58,963
They're coming. Keep moving.

433
00:43:00,272 --> 00:43:02,866
MAN: Two subjects seen exiting safe house.

434
00:43:14,953 --> 00:43:15,942
What the hell is this?

435
00:43:16,693 --> 00:43:18,752
MAN: Wait, wait, wait! No, no, no!

436
00:43:25,530 --> 00:43:27,259
What the hell just happened?

437
00:43:27,365 --> 00:43:29,994
We've lost visual contact with the subjects, sir. Christ!

438
00:43:32,637 --> 00:43:36,767
Issue a standing kill order on Jason Bourne, effective immediately.

439
00:43:38,009 --> 00:43:44,413
Send out a system one alert to all Spanish contacts. I want all air and ground border exits locked down.

440
00:44:05,904 --> 00:44:07,838
What's going on?

441
00:44:09,274 --> 00:44:11,265
What's Daniels got?

442
00:44:12,677 --> 00:44:14,804
What's Operation Black briar?

443
00:44:16,882 --> 00:44:20,613
Do you want to tell me, or should I call Kramer and ask him?

444
00:44:24,389 --> 00:44:26,482
For Christ's sake, Pam, we're in the middle of an operation.

445
00:44:26,591 --> 00:44:28,252
Bullshit.

446
00:44:29,127 --> 00:44:31,095
You want Jason Bourne,

447
00:44:32,063 --> 00:44:33,792
level with me.

448
00:44:41,573 --> 00:44:45,373
Operation Black briar started as an NEAT surveillance program.

449
00:44:45,477 --> 00:44:46,637
And what is it now?

450
00:44:46,745 --> 00:44:50,044
It is now the umbrella program for all our black ops.

451
00:44:50,148 --> 00:44:53,879
Full envelope intrusion, rendition, experimental interrogation

452
00:44:53,985 --> 00:44:56,249
is all run out of this office.

453
00:44:58,223 --> 00:45:01,351
We are the sharp end of the stick now, Pam.

454
00:45:01,459 --> 00:45:03,393
Lethal action?

455
00:45:03,962 --> 00:45:05,953
If we have to, sure.

456
00:45:07,065 --> 00:45:10,466
That's what makes us special. No more red tape.

457
00:45:11,436 --> 00:45:13,495
No more getting the bad guys caught in our sights,

458
00:45:13,605 --> 00:45:14,833
then watching them escape

459
00:45:14,940 --> 00:45:17,067
while we wait for someone in Washington to issue the order.

460
00:45:18,610 --> 00:45:20,339
Oh, come on.

461
00:45:21,780 --> 00:45:25,307
You've seen the raw intel, Pam. You know how real the danger is.

462
00:45:25,417 --> 00:45:27,908
We need these programs now.

463
00:45:28,019 --> 00:45:29,953
What's the connection to Daniels?

464
00:45:30,055 --> 00:45:33,718
He ran all of our operations in Southern Europe and North Africa,

465
00:45:33,825 --> 00:45:35,292
so he has everything.

466
00:45:35,360 --> 00:45:39,023
Names, dates, ghost sites, who's cooperating with us abroad.

467
00:45:39,130 --> 00:45:40,961
Every operation.

468
00:45:41,066 --> 00:45:43,864
You want that stuff in Bourne's hands, out on the market to the highest bidder?

469
00:45:43,969 --> 00:45:45,698
I don't think so.

470
00:45:47,505 --> 00:45:51,134
Bourne's not after money. He's after Daniels for a reason.

471
00:45:51,977 --> 00:45:54,537
Well, what does it matter what Bourne is after?

472
00:45:54,646 --> 00:45:58,013
When we find Daniels, and, believe me, we'll find him,

473
00:45:58,116 --> 00:45:59,981
if you're right,

474
00:46:00,485 --> 00:46:02,350
we get Bourne, too.

475
00:46:31,049 --> 00:46:32,983
Why did you come back?

476
00:46:35,186 --> 00:46:37,518
Why are you looking for Daniels?

477
00:46:47,232 --> 00:46:49,223
Do you know who that is?

478
00:46:50,669 --> 00:46:52,398
That's Daniels.

479
00:46:54,105 --> 00:46:56,630
I don't know who that is. Who is he?

480
00:47:02,347 --> 00:47:04,577
He was there at the beginning.

481
00:47:05,717 --> 00:47:07,708
I remember meeting him.

482
00:47:10,221 --> 00:47:11,779
The first day.

483
00:47:11,890 --> 00:47:13,915
Daniels brought me to him.

484
00:47:16,628 --> 00:47:18,960
That's where it all started for me.

485
00:47:19,698 --> 00:47:23,566
Something happened to me and I need to know what it was

486
00:47:25,670 --> 00:47:28,138
or I'll never be free of this.

487
00:47:29,007 --> 00:47:31,874
Daniels said the training was experimental.

488
00:47:34,713 --> 00:47:36,613
Behavior modification.

489
00:47:37,716 --> 00:47:41,345
They had to break down the agents before they became operational.

490
00:47:43,121 --> 00:47:45,419
He said you were the first one.

491
00:47:48,560 --> 00:47:50,528
Why are you helping me?

492
00:48:01,373 --> 00:48:03,398
It was difficult for me

493
00:48:05,043 --> 00:48:06,704
with you.

494
00:48:22,193 --> 00:48:24,684
You really don't remember anything.

495
00:48:28,733 --> 00:48:30,257
No.

496
00:48:38,443 --> 00:48:40,172
We have to move.

497
00:48:49,721 --> 00:48:52,952
Sir? Mr. Wills? You're gonna want to look at this.

498
00:49:03,802 --> 00:49:05,531
WILLS: He's in Tangier.

499
00:49:12,377 --> 00:49:14,038
Noah Vosen.

500
00:49:23,221 --> 00:49:25,086
We have found Daniels.

501
00:49:29,694 --> 00:49:32,492
They've just tracked Daniels' passport to a hotel in Tangier.

502
00:49:32,597 --> 00:49:34,462
They're holding up a bank transfer he made to keep him in place

503
00:49:34,566 --> 00:49:37,262
while they bring an asset up from Casablanca.

504
00:49:37,368 --> 00:49:38,835
They're gonna take him out.

505
00:49:48,012 --> 00:49:50,207
Yeah. WOMAN: It's Pam Landy. She says it's urgent.

506
00:49:52,050 --> 00:49:54,541
Tell her I'm unavailable. Yes, sir.

507
00:50:49,274 --> 00:50:51,572
BRIAN: Sir, asset has arrived at the airport.

508
00:51:13,831 --> 00:51:16,299
Give me the subject's location.

509
00:51:16,367 --> 00:51:19,598
MAN: Subject is now on foot and entering Hotel Velasquez.

510
00:51:19,704 --> 00:51:22,571
Hotel is 2.2 kilometers from the bank.

511
00:51:23,608 --> 00:51:26,771
All right, get an elevation and a floor plan, tic-tac-toe.

512
00:51:26,878 --> 00:51:27,970
Locate the room.

513
00:51:28,079 --> 00:51:31,515
Give the asset subject location and the route between the subject's hotel and the bank.

514
00:51:48,233 --> 00:51:51,532
VOSEN: Do we have that room yet? MAN: Yes, sir. It's room 117.

515
00:51:52,170 --> 00:51:54,502
All right, get a hold of the hotel trunk line.

516
00:51:54,606 --> 00:51:58,269
Run all calls through here with an ISO on room 117.

517
00:52:11,823 --> 00:52:14,053
His location's being blocked by the firewall.

518
00:52:14,158 --> 00:52:16,558
No, they found Daniels. They know where he is.

519
00:52:16,661 --> 00:52:18,458
They'll get one of the operatives to terminate him.

520
00:52:18,563 --> 00:52:20,224
Find out who.

521
00:52:23,935 --> 00:52:25,459
NICKY: Desh.

522
00:52:27,905 --> 00:52:30,806
Tell him you're gonna meet him and you have a new phone for him.

523
00:52:30,908 --> 00:52:33,035
If you stop Desh, they'll just get someone else.

524
00:52:33,144 --> 00:52:34,941
No, we're not gonna stop him, we're gonna follow him.

525
00:52:35,046 --> 00:52:36,445
He'll take us right to Daniels.

526
00:53:14,686 --> 00:53:17,382
Sir, the asset is deviating off course.

527
00:53:19,824 --> 00:53:21,223
Let it play.

528
00:53:53,591 --> 00:53:55,491
Asset unscheduled stop.

529
00:54:26,190 --> 00:54:29,023
Sir, asset is on the move en route to subject.

530
00:54:29,127 --> 00:54:31,254
WILLS: Sir, we have an unauthorized breach.

531
00:54:31,362 --> 00:54:34,525
Someone with active system knowledge penetrated our protocol.

532
00:54:34,632 --> 00:54:38,466
Instructions were sent to the asset at 1411 local time.

533
00:54:38,569 --> 00:54:43,608
Trace is confirmed and valid. It came from a computer belonging to Nicky Parsons.

534
00:54:47,211 --> 00:54:49,042
Where did the course deviation occur?

535
00:54:49,147 --> 00:54:51,707
South to Rue de Belgique, stationary Place de France.

536
00:54:52,917 --> 00:54:54,942
That's where Parsons is.

537
00:54:55,052 --> 00:54:57,282
When we're finished with Daniels, send the asset after her.

538
00:54:57,388 --> 00:54:58,355
MAN: Yes, sir.

539
00:54:58,456 --> 00:55:00,651
We find Parsons, we find Bourne.

540
00:55:00,758 --> 00:55:02,749
Noah, what are you doing?

541
00:55:02,960 --> 00:55:04,860
Not now. I wanna know what's going on.

542
00:55:04,962 --> 00:55:06,122
I said not now!

543
00:55:06,230 --> 00:55:08,494
What basis are you continuing this operation on?

544
00:55:08,599 --> 00:55:11,397
On the basis that Nicky Parsons has compromised a covert operation.

545
00:55:11,502 --> 00:55:14,403
She is up to her neck in this! This is about Daniels, not Nicky!

546
00:55:14,505 --> 00:55:17,338
She has betrayed us. You don't know the circumstances, Noah.

547
00:55:17,442 --> 00:55:19,205
She's in league with Jason Bourne, for Christ's sakes!

548
00:55:19,310 --> 00:55:22,143
You do not have the authority to kill her!

549
00:55:22,246 --> 00:55:25,306
Oh, yes, I do. And you had better get on board.

550
00:55:25,416 --> 00:55:27,350
Noah, she's one of us.

551
00:55:27,452 --> 00:55:30,421
You start down this path, where does it end?

552
00:55:31,088 --> 00:55:33,079
It ends when we've won.

553
00:55:46,437 --> 00:55:49,338
When we're finished with Daniels, send the asset after them.

554
00:55:49,440 --> 00:55:52,705
Yes, sir. MAN 1: Okay, come on. MAN 2: Stand by...

555
00:56:13,197 --> 00:56:17,400
Two minutes, sir. Two minutes. Tell the bank to release the funds.

556
00:56:33,985 --> 00:56:36,681
(WOMAN SPEAKING FRENCH)

557
00:56:42,093 --> 00:56:43,958
He's on the move.

558
00:57:21,770 --> 00:57:22,862
On it, sir.

559
00:57:23,868 --> 00:57:25,961
MAN 1: Two hundred meters. MAN 2: Okay, come on, I want to lay in some preliminary tracking.

560
00:57:36,247 --> 00:57:37,839
Stop!

561
00:58:00,504 --> 00:58:03,405
(BEEPING)

562
01:09:19,483 --> 01:09:21,781
Code it in. We need to be dead.

563
01:09:29,660 --> 01:09:32,493
Sir? Asset confirms both targets are down.

564
01:09:43,073 --> 01:09:44,563
I want to be sure about this.

565
01:09:44,675 --> 01:09:46,734
Ask the station chief from Rabat to confirm the deaths

566
01:09:46,843 --> 01:09:50,625
and do a sub-rosa collection of the bodies. I want to tie this thing off completely.

567
01:09:50,714 --> 01:09:52,739
And keep an eye on Landy.

568
01:10:04,027 --> 01:10:05,961
VOSEN: Bourne and Nicky Parsons are dead.

569
01:10:06,229 --> 01:10:07,526
You sure about that?

570
01:10:07,631 --> 01:10:10,464
Our station chief in Rabat is confirming.

571
01:10:11,935 --> 01:10:14,403
I can't afford to have this come back to me.

572
01:10:15,372 --> 01:10:17,602
Don't worry. You're protected.

573
01:10:18,041 --> 01:10:20,669
Just remember why we put Landy there.

574
01:10:21,745 --> 01:10:26,772
If Black briar goes south, we'll roll it up, hang it around her neck and start over.

575
01:11:35,218 --> 01:11:37,152
I can see their faces.

576
01:11:43,093 --> 01:11:45,220
Everyone I ever killed.

577
01:11:47,697 --> 01:11:49,927
I just don't know their names.

578
01:12:05,649 --> 01:12:07,549
Marie used to try to

579
01:12:10,187 --> 01:12:12,314
help me remember the names.

580
01:12:24,868 --> 01:12:29,823
I've tried to apologize for... For what I've done.

581
01:12:33,610 --> 01:12:35,601
For what I am.

582
01:12:38,048 --> 01:12:40,346
None of it makes it any better.

583
01:12:56,566 --> 01:12:58,966
They're gonna come for you again.

584
01:13:03,974 --> 01:13:06,169
You're gonna have to run now.

585
01:14:30,126 --> 01:14:31,855
We should go.

586
01:15:00,490 --> 01:15:02,424
It gets easier.

587
01:15:18,608 --> 01:15:22,009
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

588
01:15:22,112 --> 01:15:23,670
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

589
01:16:04,054 --> 01:16:06,522
Station chief in Rabat just called.

590
01:16:06,623 --> 01:16:08,557
They found a body.

591
01:16:10,827 --> 01:16:12,818
Bourne? Desh.

592
01:16:19,703 --> 01:16:21,728
Pam. You need to see this.

593
01:16:29,379 --> 01:16:32,177
A passport for Gilberto de Piento just cleared immigration.

594
01:16:32,282 --> 01:16:35,115
It's an early Tread stone identity registered to Jason Bourne,

595
01:16:35,218 --> 01:16:37,880
but he never used it, and it never went to the grid.

596
01:16:38,922 --> 01:16:40,651
Bourne's alive.

597
01:16:48,098 --> 01:16:49,087
They don't know?

598
01:16:49,199 --> 01:16:52,168
Well, if they knew, Vosen wouldn't be in his office right now.

599
01:16:52,268 --> 01:16:53,735
It's a hell of a risk.

600
01:16:55,038 --> 01:16:57,506
Maybe Bourne wants us to know.

601
01:16:57,574 --> 01:17:00,941
Just like Naples. Maybe he's communicating.

602
01:17:02,178 --> 01:17:04,169
Maybe he's trying to communicate with you.

603
01:17:04,280 --> 01:17:06,578
Then we should communicate back.

604
01:17:07,584 --> 01:17:09,552
I think I know what Bourne's looking for.

605
01:17:17,994 --> 01:17:20,827
MAN ON PA: Gilberto de Piento. Gilberto de Piento.

606
01:17:20,930 --> 01:17:23,194
Your party is waiting for you.

607
01:18:55,592 --> 01:18:57,059
Pamela Landy.

608
01:18:57,160 --> 01:18:59,685
I hear you're still looking for me.

609
01:19:02,565 --> 01:19:03,691
Bourne?

610
01:19:03,800 --> 01:19:07,253
What do you want? (TELEPHONE BEEPING)

611
01:19:09,973 --> 01:19:12,134
Yeah? WILLS O VER INTERCOM: Better get in here. We got a situation.

612
01:19:13,209 --> 01:19:14,733
I...

613
01:19:15,945 --> 01:19:18,641
I wanted to thank you for the tape.

614
01:19:19,983 --> 01:19:23,009
LAND Y ON SPEAKER: It's all tied off. It's over.

615
01:19:23,119 --> 01:19:25,280
I guess I owe you an apology.

616
01:19:26,623 --> 01:19:28,386
Is that official?

617
01:19:28,491 --> 01:19:31,324
No. Off the record. You know how it is.

618
01:19:31,427 --> 01:19:33,974
You tracing this? MAN: Fifty seconds to trace.

619
01:19:34,063 --> 01:19:35,997
Goodbye. Wait. Wait.

620
01:19:38,801 --> 01:19:41,201
David Webb. That's your real name.

621
01:19:43,239 --> 01:19:47,039
You were born 4/15/71 in Nixa, Missouri.

622
01:19:47,844 --> 01:19:50,836
Why don't you come in and we'll talk about it?

623
01:19:51,781 --> 01:19:53,976
Something is very wrong here.

624
01:19:56,319 --> 01:19:57,911
Bourne?

625
01:19:59,656 --> 01:20:01,123
Get some rest, Pam.

626
01:20:01,190 --> 01:20:03,055
You look tired.

627
01:20:05,094 --> 01:20:07,119
He's looking right at her.

628
01:20:10,166 --> 01:20:11,224
People, listen up!

629
01:20:11,334 --> 01:20:15,259
This is a national security emergency. We have an imminent threat.

630
01:20:15,338 --> 01:20:16,965
I'm going out there.

631
01:20:17,073 --> 01:20:19,405
If I show myself, he'll find me.

632
01:20:19,509 --> 01:20:22,342
Jason Bourne is alive and is at large in New York City,

633
01:20:22,445 --> 01:20:24,811
and, we believe, within 1,000 yards of this building.

634
01:20:24,914 --> 01:20:27,576
I want an immediate 12-block lockdown of the area.

635
01:20:27,684 --> 01:20:31,620
Send a flash message to Langley. Prep for local backup assistance.

636
01:20:33,756 --> 01:20:36,816
Landy just left the building! Stay with her phone.

637
01:20:53,609 --> 01:20:56,703
She's using her cell. There's an incoming text.

638
01:20:56,813 --> 01:20:58,007
Get it. MAN: Working on it, sir.

639
01:20:58,114 --> 01:21:00,431
How many do we have on Landy? Six men. More on the way.

640
01:21:00,516 --> 01:21:03,747
I've got it, sir! Coming up on the screen now.

641
01:21:07,523 --> 01:21:10,720
Anybody not on Landy goes directly to Tudor City.

642
01:21:10,827 --> 01:21:13,295
Get the vehicles. We're going mobile.

643
01:21:15,098 --> 01:21:16,395
Team Two. Team Two. All teams, call in.

644
01:21:52,557 --> 01:21:54,115
178th.

645
01:21:58,574 --> 01:22:00,269
There's only one way out of there. Why would he do that?

646
01:22:00,376 --> 01:22:01,638
He's trapping himself.

647
01:22:01,744 --> 01:22:03,473
It's a bad place to meet. It's too exposed.

648
01:22:03,579 --> 01:22:05,479
He wouldn't have chosen it if he didn't have a reason.

649
01:22:11,554 --> 01:22:13,613
Subject is en route.

650
01:22:13,723 --> 01:22:15,623
MAN: Roof 43, let me know when you have visual.

651
01:22:15,725 --> 01:22:17,659
Roof 43, standing by.

652
01:22:24,200 --> 01:22:25,189
Standing by.

653
01:22:25,301 --> 01:22:28,634
Okay, folks, here we go. Box 200 meters.

654
01:22:28,738 --> 01:22:30,035
Visual on leader.

655
01:22:30,139 --> 01:22:32,437
43 ground in position.

656
01:22:32,942 --> 01:22:35,638
As soon as you have eyes on Landy, I wanna know.

657
01:22:50,259 --> 01:22:51,385
Okay, here we go.

658
01:22:51,494 --> 01:22:53,428
Copy that. I see her.

659
01:23:05,374 --> 01:23:07,308
Any sign of Bourne?

660
01:23:07,410 --> 01:23:08,934
MAN: Negative.

661
01:23:09,745 --> 01:23:11,610
MAN 2: No sign of target.

662
01:23:22,859 --> 01:23:24,724
Noah Vosen.

663
01:23:25,328 --> 01:23:27,193
This is Jason Bourne.

664
01:23:28,097 --> 01:23:30,759
I was wondering when you were going to make this call.

665
01:23:30,867 --> 01:23:32,391
How did you get this number?

666
01:23:32,502 --> 01:23:36,370
You didn't actually think I was coming to Tudor City, did you?

667
01:23:38,374 --> 01:23:39,864
No, I guess not.

668
01:23:39,976 --> 01:23:44,368
But if it's me you want to talk to, perhaps we can arrange a meet.

669
01:23:44,447 --> 01:23:46,312
Where are you now?

670
01:23:47,083 --> 01:23:49,108
I'm sitting in my office.

671
01:23:50,520 --> 01:23:52,181
I doubt that.

672
01:23:52,555 --> 01:23:54,352
And why would you doubt that?

673
01:23:54,457 --> 01:23:55,856
If you were in your office right now,

674
01:23:55,958 --> 01:23:58,984
we'd be having this conversation face to face.

675
01:24:06,002 --> 01:24:07,663
(ON RECORDER) Noah Vosen.

676
01:24:10,439 --> 01:24:12,134
This is a code ten abort.

677
01:24:12,241 --> 01:24:14,539
I want everyone back in the vehicles. This is a code ten abort.

678
01:24:14,644 --> 01:24:16,373
MAN: Let's go! Let's go!

679
01:24:39,024 --> 01:24:43,255
Yeah? Wills, check my office. (PEOPLE CHATTERING)

680
01:24:46,209 --> 01:24:48,892
Damn it! VOSEN: What's going on?

681
01:24:51,914 --> 01:24:54,382
We need building security up here.

682
01:24:55,651 --> 01:24:57,482
He's got everything. God damn it!

683
01:24:57,587 --> 01:24:59,646
All right, set a four-block perimeter around the building.

684
01:24:59,755 --> 01:25:01,017
MAN: Somebody give me a visual.

685
01:25:01,123 --> 01:25:02,488
I want the entire building searched.

686
01:25:02,592 --> 01:25:05,925
Every room, every hallway, every closet, every goddamn air duct.

687
01:25:06,028 --> 01:25:07,996
You understand? I want him found!

688
01:25:11,667 --> 01:25:12,861
What just happened?

689
01:25:12,969 --> 01:25:16,427
Bourne just broke into CRI. He got into Vosen's safe.

690
01:25:18,441 --> 01:25:19,601
Where to?

691
01:25:19,709 --> 01:25:22,007
415 East 71st Street.

692
01:25:22,878 --> 01:25:25,870
Four-fifteen-seventy-one? Jesus, Pam.

693
01:25:51,474 --> 01:25:53,203
Target in sight.

694
01:25:57,947 --> 01:25:59,881
North on Eighth.

695
01:26:06,589 --> 01:26:08,056
He's headed east in the Port Authority.

696
01:26:08,157 --> 01:26:10,091
All agents have shoot-on-sight authorization.

697
01:27:18,961 --> 01:27:20,519
Sir, he drove off the roof. What?

698
01:27:20,629 --> 01:27:22,563
He drove off the roof!

699
01:27:23,999 --> 01:27:26,092
He's on foot. He's running.

700
01:27:36,746 --> 01:27:39,772
Police! Freeze! Put your hands in the air!

701
01:27:49,380 --> 01:27:51,007
Call for backup!

702
01:28:15,584 --> 01:28:18,280
Sir, sir, take a look at this! Bourne's birthday, sir.

703
01:28:18,387 --> 01:28:19,684
What about it? Check that out.

704
01:28:19,789 --> 01:28:23,520
Sir, Landy told Bourne that his birthday was 4l15l71.

705
01:28:23,626 --> 01:28:24,786
（ 9/13/70 ）

706
01:28:24,894 --> 01:28:26,828
Oh, my God. It's a code.

707
01:28:27,496 --> 01:28:30,090
Everything stops. Everything stops! Listen up!

708
01:28:30,199 --> 01:28:33,032
4l15l71. New assignment, numbers.

709
01:28:33,135 --> 01:28:34,966
What does it mean? Give me encryption codes!

710
01:28:35,070 --> 01:28:37,595
Sir, if you plug them in as variables of longitude and latitude

711
01:28:37,706 --> 01:28:39,435
you get Cameroon.

712
01:28:39,542 --> 01:28:42,443
41571 is the zip code for Varney, Kentucky.

713
01:28:45,381 --> 01:28:49,249
What date did she give him? WILLS: 4/15/71.

714
01:28:49,351 --> 01:28:51,080
I don't believe it.

715
01:28:51,654 --> 01:28:55,283
SRD is at 415 East 71st Street.

716
01:28:55,391 --> 01:28:58,274
She just gave him the training facility. Oh, Christ.

717
01:28:58,394 --> 01:29:00,794
Bring all the teams in behind us.

718
01:30:59,237 --> 01:31:00,932
Hurry up! Somebody call 911!

719
01:31:01,005 --> 01:31:02,029
Help him!

720
01:31:36,418 --> 01:31:38,943
WILLS: The asset lost Bourne. We lost him.

721
01:31:47,997 --> 01:31:49,931
Hello? Albert, it's Vosen.

722
01:31:50,499 --> 01:31:54,162
Bourne knows everything and he's on his way to you right now.

723
01:31:54,737 --> 01:31:56,932
He's coming home, Noah.

724
01:31:57,039 --> 01:32:00,133
How long do I have? I don't know.

725
01:32:00,242 --> 01:32:02,574
Just get the hell out of there.

726
01:32:02,711 --> 01:32:04,645
No, I'm gonna stay.

727
01:32:04,747 --> 01:32:08,239
He'll head for the training wing. That's what he knows.

728
01:32:08,550 --> 01:32:12,316
I'll keep him in play till you get there.

729
01:33:03,539 --> 01:33:05,530
They'll kill you for giving me this.

730
01:33:05,641 --> 01:33:08,508
4l15l71 isn't much of a code.

731
01:33:08,610 --> 01:33:11,374
My guess is Vosen is on his way already.

732
01:33:12,347 --> 01:33:14,144
Why'd you do it?

733
01:33:14,249 --> 01:33:18,686
Because this isn't what I signed up for, what they did to you, Black briar.

734
01:33:19,154 --> 01:33:21,088
This isn't us.

735
01:33:22,691 --> 01:33:26,388
Then do something about it. Everything you need is in there.

736
01:33:30,666 --> 01:33:32,531
Everything.

737
01:33:33,435 --> 01:33:36,666
David. Why don't you come in with me?

738
01:33:36,772 --> 01:33:39,707
It'll be better if we do this together. No.

739
01:33:41,643 --> 01:33:46,133
This is where it started for me. This is where it ends.

740
01:33:59,328 --> 01:34:01,057
That's Landy.

741
01:34:13,242 --> 01:34:17,702
All right, lock this building down. Set a secure perimeter of one block.

742
01:34:23,652 --> 01:34:27,053
Hello. This is Pamela Landy. I have to send a classified document.

743
01:34:27,156 --> 01:34:28,953
Get a team to SRD after Bourne.

744
01:34:29,057 --> 01:34:30,820
And put someone in every public area of this hospital.

745
01:34:30,926 --> 01:34:33,918
Okay. Elevator shafts, service entrances, go!

746
01:34:39,268 --> 01:34:41,862
Damn it! South bay! Go!

747
01:34:42,404 --> 01:34:45,703
Gentlemen, this is a priority one situation! You will give us your full cooperation.

748
01:34:45,808 --> 01:34:47,935
Give me playback for the entire building for the last three minutes.

749
01:34:48,043 --> 01:34:49,704
Yes, sir.

750
01:35:00,811 --> 01:35:02,244
Move! Move!

751
01:35:07,963 --> 01:35:11,228
This one, here! Where is this? First floor.

752
01:35:11,333 --> 01:35:13,392
I'll take Landy on my own.

753
01:35:48,770 --> 01:35:51,432
You better get yourself a good lawyer.

754
01:36:05,354 --> 01:36:08,619
DR. HIRSCH: A republic lives on the knife's edge.

755
01:36:16,531 --> 01:36:20,490
When we are finished with you, you will no longer be David Webb.

756
01:36:22,971 --> 01:36:25,804
You may not even remember who he was.

757
01:36:28,410 --> 01:36:31,436
You know why we're treating you like this?

758
01:36:33,181 --> 01:36:35,695
Hello, Jason. (GUN COCKING)

759
01:36:37,386 --> 01:36:40,583
I believe you've been having some problems.

760
01:36:40,689 --> 01:36:42,418
Put the gun down.

761
01:36:43,425 --> 01:36:46,360
I wouldn't be here if I didn't want to talk.

762
01:36:49,631 --> 01:36:51,929
I've spent three years running.

763
01:36:52,668 --> 01:36:55,831
Three years trying to find out who I am.

764
01:36:55,938 --> 01:36:58,839
You've still not got it all back, have you?

765
01:36:59,541 --> 01:37:03,560
Still not filled in the pieces. It was always you.

766
01:37:05,714 --> 01:37:07,477
I'm unarmed, Jason.

767
01:37:08,016 --> 01:37:10,541
Why me? Why did you pick me?

768
01:37:11,887 --> 01:37:14,549
Your really don't remember, do you?

769
01:37:16,892 --> 01:37:19,884
We didn't pick you. You picked us.

770
01:37:23,031 --> 01:37:24,896
You volunteered.

771
01:37:26,601 --> 01:37:28,330
Right here.

772
01:37:31,039 --> 01:37:32,529
Even after you were warned.

773
01:37:32,641 --> 01:37:33,938
(LOCK CLICKING)

774
01:37:42,651 --> 01:37:44,448
Captain Webb.

775
01:37:44,553 --> 01:37:45,815
Good morning, Captain.

776
01:37:51,393 --> 01:37:53,384
You came in here.

777
01:37:55,497 --> 01:37:58,295
You didn't even blink, Jason.

778
01:38:03,438 --> 01:38:05,463
You just handed me these.

779
01:38:12,347 --> 01:38:14,838
DR. HIRSCH: Has everything been explained to you?

780
01:38:16,651 --> 01:38:18,380
Yes, sir.

781
01:38:20,589 --> 01:38:22,853
You said you wanted to serve.

782
01:38:24,593 --> 01:38:29,516
Your missions will save American lives. WEBB: I understand, sir.

783
01:38:32,200 --> 01:38:34,828
You said I'd be saving American lives.

784
01:38:35,370 --> 01:38:37,031
You were.

785
01:38:37,139 --> 01:38:42,941
I was killing for you. For them.

786
01:38:43,845 --> 01:38:48,441
You knew exactly what it meant for you if you chose to stay.

787
01:38:48,750 --> 01:38:52,948
When we are finished with you, you will no longer be David Webb.

788
01:38:53,055 --> 01:38:55,250
I'll be whoever you need me to be, sir.

789
01:38:57,192 --> 01:38:59,786
You can't outrun what you did, Jason.

790
01:39:00,462 --> 01:39:03,022
You made yourself into who you are.

791
01:39:03,899 --> 01:39:06,834
Eventually you're gonna have to face the fact

792
01:39:06,935 --> 01:39:11,497
you chose right here to become Jason Bourne.

793
01:39:18,080 --> 01:39:20,548
DR. HIRSCH: You haven't slept for a long time.

794
01:39:25,887 --> 01:39:27,946
Have you made a decision?

795
01:39:32,561 --> 01:39:34,426
This can't go on.

796
01:39:34,996 --> 01:39:36,759
You have to decide.

797
01:39:40,368 --> 01:39:43,804
Who is he? We've been through that.

798
01:39:47,409 --> 01:39:49,274
What did he do?

799
01:39:49,578 --> 01:39:51,375
It doesn't matter.

800
01:40:05,227 --> 01:40:07,195
You came to us.

801
01:40:09,898 --> 01:40:11,832
You volunteered.

802
01:40:12,701 --> 01:40:15,829
You said you'd do anything it takes to

803
01:40:16,538 --> 01:40:18,665
save American lives.

804
01:40:19,341 --> 01:40:21,468
You're not a liar, are you?

805
01:40:22,544 --> 01:40:25,012
Or too weak

806
01:40:25,914 --> 01:40:27,848
to see this through?

807
01:40:29,384 --> 01:40:31,113
This is it.

808
01:40:32,053 --> 01:40:34,817
Let go of David Webb.

809
01:40:40,562 --> 01:40:44,225
Really give yourself to this program.

810
01:41:09,558 --> 01:41:11,423
You're no longer

811
01:41:12,394 --> 01:41:14,055
David Webb.

812
01:41:15,230 --> 01:41:19,360
From now on, you'll be known as Jason Bourne.

813
01:41:21,136 --> 01:41:23,263
Welcome to the program.

814
01:41:36,484 --> 01:41:38,418
Do you remember now?

815
01:41:47,095 --> 01:41:48,756
I remember.

816
01:41:50,832 --> 01:41:52,697
I remember everything.

817
01:41:54,302 --> 01:41:56,429
I'm no longer Jason Bourne.

818
01:41:58,139 --> 01:42:00,403
So now you're gonna kill me.

819
01:42:01,710 --> 01:42:03,177
No.

820
01:42:04,613 --> 01:42:08,674
You don't deserve the star they'd give you on the wall at Langley.

821
01:42:23,131 --> 01:42:25,156
MAN: He's headed for the roof!

822
01:43:10,378 --> 01:43:12,539
Why didn't you take the shot?

823
01:43:21,556 --> 01:43:24,650
Do you even know why you're supposed to kill me?

824
01:43:34,102 --> 01:43:35,763
Look at us.

825
01:43:38,540 --> 01:43:40,872
Look at what they make you give.

826
01:44:32,026 --> 01:44:33,516
Good morning, senators.

827
01:44:33,628 --> 01:44:38,588
If I may, I'd like to begin by making a statement for the record.

828
01:44:41,403 --> 01:44:46,033
The file indicates that Ezra Kramer authorized six illegal...

829
01:44:46,141 --> 01:44:49,042
REPORTER ON TV: The President convened an emergency cabinet meeting today

830
01:44:49,144 --> 01:44:53,308
to discuss the growing scandal over an alleged government assassination program,

831
01:44:53,415 --> 01:44:55,383
code-named Black briar.

832
01:44:55,483 --> 01:44:57,212
CIA Director Ezra Kramer

833
01:44:57,318 --> 01:44:58,615
is under criminal investigation

834
01:44:58,720 --> 01:45:00,551
for authorizing the program,

835
01:45:00,655 --> 01:45:04,557
which in several cases may have even targeted US citizens.

836
01:45:08,696 --> 01:45:11,426
Two agency officials have already been arrested.

837
01:45:11,533 --> 01:45:15,196
Dr. Albert Hirsch, the alleged mastermind of Black briar program

838
01:45:15,303 --> 01:45:19,797
and CIA Deputy Director Noah Vosen, the program's operational chief.

839
01:45:23,311 --> 01:45:27,582
Meanwhile, mystery surrounds the fate of David Webb, also known as Jason Bourne, the source

840
01:45:27,582 --> 01:45:30,574
behind the exposure of the Black briar program.

841
01:45:30,685 --> 01:45:34,086
It's been reported that Webb was shot and fell from a Manhattan rooftop

842
01:45:34,189 --> 01:45:36,885
